[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: KM271-WiFi Hardware Requirements
UID: KM271-HW
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Hardware requirements of the KM271-WiFi main board, revision v2.0. They
refine the system requirements (KM271-SYS-xxx) and are allocated to the
subsystems of the system architecture (KM271-SYA-xxx). Design compliance
refers to the schematic and layout state of 2026-11-24 (ESP32-S3, JP1/JP2
USB path selection, PCA9306 removed).
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Power supply

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-001
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Slot supply input
STATEMENT: >>>
The board shall take its main supply from pin 1 (+5 V) and pin 2 (GND) of the
Logamatic slot connector J1.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-012
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-100

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-002
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Decoupled supply sources
STATEMENT: >>>
USB VBUS and the slot 5 V shall be combined such that no current flows from
one source into the other, with a forward drop of at most 0.45 V at 400 mA.
<<<
COMMENT: D8/D9 1N5819WS: about 0.38 V at 290 mA.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-013
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-003
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Protection
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Transient protection of the slot input
STATEMENT: >>>
The slot 5 V input shall be protected against transients by a TVS diode with a
stand-off voltage of at least 5.0 V.
<<<
COMMENT: D10 SMAJ5.0A.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-042
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-004
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Analysis, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: 3.3 V rail
STATEMENT: >>>
The board shall provide a 3.3 V rail with a tolerance of +-3 % for a
continuous load of at least 600 mA (ESP32-S3 with WiFi peaks, extension).
<<<
COMMENT: U8 TPS62162 (1 A, fixed 3.3 V).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-005
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Simulation, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Regulation with weak source
STATEMENT: >>>
The 3.3 V rail shall stay above 3.0 V during a load step from 60 mA to 460 mA
at a slot source resistance of up to 2 Ohm.
<<<
SOURCE: DOC/Power-Analysis/README.md
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-006
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Simulation
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Efficient conversion
STATEMENT: >>>
The 3.3 V regulator should be a switching converter so that the current drawn
from the slot is lower than the 3.3 V load current.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-012
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-201

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-007
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Bulk capacitance
STATEMENT: >>>
The 5 V and 3.3 V rails shall each be buffered with low-ESR bulk capacitance
of at least 200 uF to cover WiFi transmit bursts.
<<<
COMMENT: C7/C8 220 uF / 16 V polymer.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-008
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Manufacturing
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: LDO assembly alternative
STATEMENT: >>>
The layout shall keep an LDO as not-fitted alternative to the step-down
converter. Selection shall be done by 0 Ohm resistors that cannot both be
required at the same time.
<<<
COMMENT: R78 (buck, fitted) / R79 (LDO, DNP), U2 and C4 DNP.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-201

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-009
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Could
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: External 3.3 V feed
STATEMENT: >>>
It shall be possible to supply the board with 3.3 V through J6 or J7 after
separating the on-board regulator by removing one resistor.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-010
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: 5 V supply monitor
STATEMENT: >>>
The +5V rail shall be measurable by an ADC1 input of the controller. The
divider shall keep the ADC input below 2.0 V at 6 V on +5V.
<<<
COMMENT: R5 100 kOhm / R12 47 kOhm to GPIO4 (ADC1_CH3): 1.92 V at 6 V.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-012

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Logamatic interface

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-020
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Serial level translation
STATEMENT: >>>
The serial lines to and from the Logamatic shall be translated between 3.3 V
logic of the controller and 5 V logic of the Logamatic in both directions.
<<<
COMMENT: U4 (LM_TX to GPIO18), U5 (GPIO17 to LM_RX), SN74LV1T34.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-101

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-021
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Defined idle level
STATEMENT: >>>
The serial line coming from the Logamatic shall have a defined idle (high)
level when the Logamatic does not drive it.
<<<
COMMENT: R2 10 kOhm to +5V.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-022
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Serial port of the controller
STATEMENT: >>>
The KM271 serial line shall use a hardware UART of the controller other than
UART0, on GPIO17 (TX) and GPIO18 (RX).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Pins agreed with the firmware community (Discussion #20); UART0 remains free
for logging and the CP2102N.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-023
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Manufacturing
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Configurable slot pins
STATEMENT: >>>
Every slot pin shall be connected through a 0 Ohm resistor footprint so that
the assignment can be adapted by assembly.
<<<
COMMENT: R33-R44; pins 9-12 not fitted.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-100

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-024
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Simulation, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Exhaust gas sensor conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The board shall connect the FG exhaust gas sensor to the Logamatic with the
same supply, filter and detection circuit as the original KM271 so that the
Logamatic detects the sensor without software support.
<<<
SOURCE: DOC/Abgassensor/README.md
COMMENT: R17 3.3 kOhm, R11 100 kOhm, C11 100 nF, C12 33 nF, R32 10 kOhm.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-020
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-105

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-025
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Simulation
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Exhaust gas reading below 80 degC
STATEMENT: >>>
The sensor circuit shall not distort the sensor voltage by more than 1 K
equivalent between 25 and 250 degC in the default assembly.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
With the clamping diode D5 fitted the Logamatic shows +21 K at 25 degC.
<<<
COMMENT: D5 BZX84C5V1 is DNP by default.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-020
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-011

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Controller

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-030
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Constraint
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Microcontroller module
STATEMENT: >>>
The controller shall be an ESP32-S3 module with integrated antenna, at least 8
MB flash and without octal PSRAM.
<<<
COMMENT: U1 ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N8R2 (LCSC C2913204).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-200

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-031
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: EMC
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Antenna placement
STATEMENT: >>>
The antenna area of the module shall overhang the board edge with no copper
below or beside it.
<<<
SOURCE: EMC review 2026-11-24
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-107

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-032
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Reliable power-on reset
STATEMENT: >>>
The EN input shall have an RC delay (pull-up and at least 1 uF) so that the
controller starts reliably on slow supply ramps.
<<<
COMMENT: R29 10 kOhm, C30 1 uF.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-033
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Boot mode selection
STATEMENT: >>>
IO0 shall be pulled up and be switchable to GND by a BOOT button and by the
auto-reset circuit. EN shall be switchable by a RESET button.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-024
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-030
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-016

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: USB and programming

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-034
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Selectable USB data path
STATEMENT: >>>
The USB data lines shall be connectable either to the native USB of the
controller or to a USB-UART bridge by changing solder jumpers only. The
default shall be the native USB.
<<<
COMMENT: JP1/JP2 SolderJumper_3_Bridged12: 1 = ESP32-S3 GPIO19/20, 3 = CP2102N.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-030
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-031
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-203

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-035
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Protection
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: ESD protection in the signal path
STATEMENT: >>>
D+ and D- shall pass over the pads of an ESD protection array directly behind
the USB connector, before any branch, jumper or series element.
<<<
RATIONALE: A TVS connected by a stub is ineffective at fast ESD edges.
COMMENT: >>>
U3 SRV05-4 is not flow-through: both pins of each channel are connected.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-042
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-036
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: EMC
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Series resistors in the USB lines
STATEMENT: >>>
D+ and D- shall have series resistors of 2.2 Ohm to limit ESD current and damp
ringing.
<<<
COMMENT: R69/R70.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-042
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-037
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: EMC
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Partially met
TITLE: USB signal routing
STATEMENT: >>>
D+ and D- shall be routed as a coupled, length-matched pair with a continuous
reference plane and at least 1.3 mm distance to the board edge.
<<<
SOURCE: EMC review 2026-11-24
COMMENT: >>>
Length matched with KiCad tuning patterns; 1.6 mm near the J2 shield pad,
otherwise >= 1.3 mm.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-042
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-038
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: USB-UART bridge
STATEMENT: >>>
The USB-UART bridge shall be self-powered from +3V3, detect the USB host via a
VBUS divider and connect to UART0 of the controller through series resistors
that let an external adapter on J4 override it.
<<<
COMMENT: U10 CP2102N, R71/R72 VBUS divider, R76/R77 220 Ohm.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-031
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-039
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Auto-reset into the bootloader
STATEMENT: >>>
With the USB-UART bridge path, DTR and RTS shall drive EN and IO0 through the
classic two-transistor circuit so that flashing tools can enter the bootloader
without user action.
<<<
COMMENT: Q1/Q2 SS8050.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-030
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-040
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Manufacturing
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Exposed pad of the USB-UART bridge
STATEMENT: >>>
The exposed pad of the bridge shall be connected to GND with vias in the pad.
<<<
COMMENT: Two vias since 2026-11-25.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-013

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Sensor inputs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-HW-050
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Analog inputs
STATEMENT: >>>
Three sensor inputs shall be connected to ADC1 channels of the controller and
each have an RC filter (100 nF) and a fitting position for a pull-up and a
pull-down.
<<<
RATIONALE: ADC2 cannot be used while WiFi is active.
COMMENT: J6 pins 2/4/6 to GPIO8/7/6.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-021
